      "writtenOn": "2022-05-19T08:21:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we use vector like this, and we only add new pairs here, we would still hold the old context values for the same ccid, even if the application has changed its content. It might be fine for TBS and MCS, but getCCID() will always get the first ever reported CCID for a given content type. If an application A starts with content X, then changes content to Y and application B start using content X, we would still get CCID for application A when asking for content X CCID, which is bad.\n\nSince LeAudioContextType is a bit field, I think we should replace existing entry for a given CCID to update the value.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 714,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 715,
        "endChar": 66
      },
